{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a8cedd3b3148af7b0","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hu55tLDtijPtsAPNBAaVA8","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-1000/-workspace-project/da796ddb-14b5-4081-b15a-294e50582b81/tasks/a8cedd3b3148af7b0.output","summary":"Ticket 02 is implemented and all 13 criteria are ticked. `pnpm --config.verify-deps-before-run=false nx build cinescope` succeeds. Lint passes, and the unit tests pass (8 of 8, including a new spec).\n\n**What I built** (all under `apps/cinescope/src/app/`):\n- `seat-selection/seat-selection.ts`, `.html`, `.scss`: the `/screenings/:id/seats` component. It loads the screening and then its movie, shows the title, the `Show Date:` subtitle, the seat-limit text above the auditorium and the `SCREEN` bar. An unknown id or any load failure redirects to `/`.\n- `seat-selection/auditorium.ts`: a pure layout builder. It produces 15 rows with the entrance (rows 1–10), two aisles per row, seats with their column numbers, row 1 accessible seats in columns 10–15, and 12 couches in row 15. Occupied seats are `unavailable`, and a couch is unavailable if either of its seats is occupied.\n- `seat-selection/auditorium.spec.ts`: checks the 308-element count, numbering, aisles, accessible seats, couches and occupancy.\n- `cinema-api.service.ts`: added `screening(id)` and `movie(id)`.\n- `dates.ts`: added `formatShowDate` and moved `WEEKDAY_NAMES` here from `movie-list.ts`, which now imports it.\n- `app.routes.ts`: route 2 now uses `SeatSelection`.\n\n**Not verified in a browser:** I could not render the page. The backend would not start in this sandbox (`pnpm api` hits the same dependency check, and a directly launched json-server died), and there is no browser. The ticks rest on the build, the unit spec and reading the template and styles. The 404 redirect and the real data path were not exercised live.\n\n**Choices the spec left open:**\n- The movie is loaded as the ticket asks, but its title is not shown, because the section 5 page layout has no place for it.\n- A failed movie load also redirects to `/`, the same rule section 6 uses for the summary.\n- Occupied and accessible seats are not clickable yet, but clicking is ticket 03's job. The `selected` state, the legend, the selected-seats panel, the booking in `sessionStorage` and the Cancel/Continue buttons are left for later tickets.\n\nTicket 02 has no unticked criteria. Nothing was committed.","usage":{"total_tokens":100473,"tool_uses":34,"duration_ms":216622},"uuid":"b6bcfcb7-d50f-42dc-b603-0976e69e7d30","session_id":"da796ddb-14b5-4081-b15a-294e50582b81"}
