ndbox (`pnpm api` hits the same dependency check, and a directly launched json-server died), and there is no browser. The ticks rest on the build, the unit spec and reading the template and styles. The 404 redirect and the real data path were not exercised live.\n  \n  **Choices the spec left open:**\n  - The movie is loaded as the ticket asks, but its title is not shown, because the section 5 page layout has no place for it.\n  - A failed movie load also redirects to `/`, the same rule section 6 uses for the summary.\n  - Occupied and accessible seats are not clickable yet, but clicking is ticket 03's job. The `selected` state, the legend, the selected-seats panel, the booking in `sessionStorage` and the Cancel/Continue buttons are left for later tickets.\n  \n  Ticket 02 has no unticked criteria. Nothing was committed.\nagentId: a8cedd3b3148af7b0 (use SendMessage with to: 'a8cedd3b3148af7b0', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 100147\ntool_uses: 34\nduration_ms: 216626</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da796ddb-14b5-4081-b15a-294e50582b81","uuid":"03c430c6-99f2-4510-9d0a-8696429fe0d6","timestamp":"2026-11-27T15:28:48.268Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are implementing one ticket of a cinema seat-booking Angular app in the Nx workspace at /workspace/project (Nx project `cinescope`, apps/cinescope). Tickets 01 is already done; build on its code. Read spec/stack.md, spec/tickets/README.md, the ticket file spec/tickets/02-auditorium-map.md, and the sections of spec/README.md that the ticket references (read spec/README.md fully if unsure; it is the complete specification). Do not ask questions; where the spec is silent choose the simplest option that satisfies it. Implement everything the ticket requires, tick the boxes in the ticket file as each acceptance criterion is satisfied (only when truly satisfied), and make sure the build succeeds. NOTE: plain `pnpm nx ...` aborts in this