{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"af0551bf40e6765a1","tool_use_id":"toolu_01LAHPDUEtcGHrTrK67tgyiY","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-1000/-workspace-project/da796ddb-14b5-4081-b15a-294e50582b81/tasks/af0551bf40e6765a1.output","summary":"Ticket 03 is implemented and all 14 of its criteria are ticked. `pnpm --config.verify-deps-before-run=false nx build cinescope` succeeds. Lint passes and the 8 existing unit tests pass.\n\n**What was built**\n- **Selection** (`seat-selection/seat-selection.ts`): seats and couches toggle on click. Unavailable ones are ignored. A couch selects or deselects both of its seats together. The 10-seat cap counts a couch as 2. A click that would exceed the cap shows the toast; deselecting is always allowed. Selection resets when a different screening is loaded.\n- **Seats and couches** (`seat-selection.html`): now `<button>` elements with `data-state` set to `available`, `selected`, `unavailable` or `accessible`. Selected is `#F9A825`, with dark text for contrast. The other colours are unchanged.\n- **Legend**: four `legend-item`s (`Available`, `Selected`, `Unavailable`, `Accessible`) under the auditorium.\n- **Selected-seats panel**: `Selected seats: <n>` plus one `Row <r>: …` line per row with a selection. It updates on every click.\n- **Cancel / Continue** buttons, using Material buttons. Continue is disabled when nothing is selected.\n- **Toast** (`app/toast.ts`, new): a Material `MatSnackBar` wrapper with `data-testid=\"toast\"`, a 4-second duration, and one toast at a time.\n- **Auditorium helper** (`seat-selection/auditorium.ts`): added `seatIdsOf` for seats and couches.\n\n**Unticked criteria:** none.\n\n**Not verified in a browser.** I didn't run the app or click through it. The criteria are checked against the code and the spec, not against a live run.\n\n**Left for later tickets**\n- Cancel has no click handler yet, since its behaviour belongs to ticket 04 (AC-33).\n- Selection lives in component state only. It is not saved in the booking, so it doesn't survive a reload yet.\n\n**Build note:** the production build prints a bundle-size budget warning (647.91 kB against a 500 kB budget). It comes from the Material bundle, not this ticket, and the build still succeeds.\n\nNothing was committed.","usage":{"total_tokens":83473,"tool_uses":17,"duration_ms":110265},"uuid":"b2128be5-6f66-47e6-923b-586cc238d862","session_id":"da796ddb-14b5-4081-b15a-294e50582b81"}
