{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"af1da784b4c4fea3e","tool_use_id":"toolu_01JPTxWcsTTxeiKsr6MdEebt","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-1000/-workspace-project/da796ddb-14b5-4081-b15a-294e50582b81/tasks/af1da784b4c4fea3e.output","summary":"Ticket 04 is implemented, and `pnpm --config.verify-deps-before-run=false nx build cinescope` succeeds. Nothing was committed.\n\n**What I built**\n- **Booking (`apps/cinescope/src/app/booking.ts`)**: a `BookingStore` that keeps `{ screeningId, seats }` in `sessionStorage`. `ticketsFor()` turns seat identifiers into summary items ordered by row and column, pairing row-15 columns as couches. A `bookingInProgressGuard` redirects to `/` unless the booking matches the screening in the URL and has at least one seat.\n- **Pricing (`pricing.ts`)**: `seatPrice(row)` gives 25/32/39 PLN, couches are 89 PLN, and `formatPrice()` gives `25.00 PLN`.\n- **Seat map**: the selection is restored from the booking when it belongs to the same screening, otherwise a new empty booking replaces the old one after the screening loads. Every selection change is persisted. `Cancel` clears the booking and goes to `/`. `Continue` goes to the summary and does nothing when no seat is selected.\n- **Summary (`summary/summary.ts`, `.html`, `.scss`)**: title `Your tickets`, one item per seat or couch with the movie title, `<date> <time>`, row, seat description, price and `Remove`, then `Total: … PLN`, `Back` and `Confirm`. `Remove` updates the booking and total, and removing the last item goes to the seat map.\n- **Routes**: the summary and checkout routes use the guard. `CinemaApi.screeningWithMovie()` is shared by the seat map and the summary. `COUCH_ROW` is now exported from `auditorium.ts`.\n- **Tests**: a new `booking.spec.ts` covers the ticket derivation, couch pairing and prices.\n\n**Checks**\n- Build: succeeds. It prints a warning that the initial bundle exceeds the 500 kB budget (653 kB raw). That is a warning, not an e